    "title": "Hillsboro Hops to partner with Adidas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Emma Watkins No media credit provided. ,\n57 minutes ago\nPORTLAND, Ore. (KOIN) — The Hillsboro Hops announced Wednesday a new partnership with Adidas, whose North American headquarters is located in the Rose City.\nThey agreed to terms which would make Adidas the fifth founding partner for the new ballpark opening in April 2026 for the Hops Opening Day game.\nHillsboro Hops President K.L. Wombacher shared at a press conference that they “are incredibly grateful for Adidas’ investment in the Hillsboro Hops and our community. Partnering with such a globally respected brand not only enhances the experience for our fans, but also reflects the bright future of Hops baseball.”\nAdidas is one of the leaders in sporting goods around the world. Adidas North America President John Miller added that “Adidas is proud to partner with the Hops in this exciting new chapter. We are eager to elevate local talent, celebrate the new venue, and deepen our commitment to our community.”\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KOIN.com.",
